steps.body:
A `switch` compares one value against constant `case` labels and jumps to the match. `break` ends the case and leaves the switch. `default` runs for every value no case lists.

```java
switch (day) {
    case 1:
        name = "Sunday";
        break;
    case 2:
        name = "Monday";
        break;
    default:
        name = "Not a day";
}
```

You can switch on `int`, `char`, `String`, and a few other types, but not on `double`, `long`, or `boolean`. Each label must be a constant, and two labels cannot repeat.

If a variable is set inside the switch, every path must set it before you read it. A `default` that assigns covers all the other values, so the compiler accepts `String name;` without a starting value.

example.code:
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int day = 3;
        String name;
        switch (day) {
            case 1:
                name = "Sunday";
                break;
            case 2:
                name = "Monday";
                break;
            case 3:
                name = "Tuesday";
                break;
            case 4:
                name = "Wednesday";
                break;
            case 5:
                name = "Thursday";
                break;
            case 6:
                name = "Friday";
                break;
            case 7:
                name = "Saturday";
                break;
            default:
                name = "Not a day";
        }
        System.out.println("Day " + day + ": " + name);

        day = 9;
        switch (day) {
            case 1:
                name = "Sunday";
                break;
            case 2:
                name = "Monday";
                break;
            case 3:
                name = "Tuesday";
                break;
            case 4:
                name = "Wednesday";
                break;
            case 5:
                name = "Thursday";
                break;
            case 6:
                name = "Friday";
                break;
            case 7:
                name = "Saturday";
                break;
            default:
                name = "Not a day";
        }
        System.out.println("Day " + day + ": " + name);
    }
}

